{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7a626d37fbb1451998d1775d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/68f6dc544b20d34dc971cbdd30ee6cf904939238cb203a413a1e7e197ce609f5.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task container-recipe: Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"container\\\",\\\"results/receipts\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:0c46252d34cfce48345e6011f6c265a64358190c531b61d7c70f49eca1aa3f2f\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n container/build.sh && grep -q 'torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'mecattaf/vllm' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'flashnext:dev' container/build.sh && grep -qi 'MIT' container/Containerfile\"],\"description\":\"The recipe pins the exact wheel set, the fork branch, and the image tag, and is syntax-clean.\",\"id\":\"recipe-pins\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"A reproducible image build from the fork at the exactly pinned wheel set\",\"A build receipt the receipts gate can grade\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"THE PRIMARY ENGINE LANE of spec ruling P4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). Write container/Containerfile and container/build.sh implementing IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. Containerfile: Ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for GPU target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\\\"build\\\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. Credit the recipe shape to the MIT toolbox recipe named in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the Containerfile header. Boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.\",\"id\":\"container-recipe\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3\",\"IMPORTS.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:6e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361\",\"title\":\"Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"a428fee66b83d95682b418d5fdb4d975068e66ab\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-96facee9fb96/container-recipe\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/container-recipe-6e8621b55de3a3a9\",\"taskId\":\"container-recipe\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/96facee9fb96/container-recipe\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER ADVISORY (arm-time): (1) A warm local wheel cache exists at /home/tom/.cache/flashnext-wheels/ on the coordinator with torch-2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, torchvision-0.28.0+rocm7.14.0, and triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0 cp312 linux_x86_64 wheels pre-downloaded from the vendor index. Your Containerfile must still reference https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (the acceptance grep requires it), but build.sh may bind-mount the cache dir and pass --find-links to pip so the multi-GB torch wheel is not re-downloaded at image build. (2) ubuntu:24.04 base image is already pulled locally via podman. (3) Do not add torchaudio — drop audio extras (the goal text is authoritative). (4) The build must ride ethernet (default route); never touch a 10.99.0.x address.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/2\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[2],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":1,\"recheckedCursor\":3,\"registrationId\":\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[{\"attempt\":1,\"comment\":\"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/1\",\"diagnosis\":\"Failed the ownership check conflict-domains because the task run left untracked artifacts under the repo-root path .build/, which is outside the authorized prefixes container and results/receipts: container/build.sh defaults CCACHE_DIR_HOST to \\\"$REPO_ROOT/.build/ccache\\\" and PIP_CACHE_HOST to \\\"$REPO_ROOT/.build/pip-cache\\\", then mkdir -p creates them inside the worktree, and the attempt also dropped .build/build.log there; git status shows the whole .build/ tree as untracked, so the driver reported \\\"agent left uncommitted changes\\\" and the ownership gate rejected the attempt. The committed source files themselves (container/Containerfile, container/build.sh, container/rootfs/.keep, results/receipts/build.json at d89f338) are all inside the boundary, so the defect is confined to where the script materializes caches and logs plus the leftover working-tree state. Fix on attempt 2, touching only container/build.sh: (1) default the host cache paths outside the repository — e.g. CCACHE_DIR_HOST=\\\"${FN_CCACHE_DIR:-${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/flashnext/ccache}\\\" and PIP_CACHE_HOST=\\\"${FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR:-${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/flashnext/pip}\\\" — keeping the FN_CCACHE_DIR / FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR overrides and the same podman --volume wiring so the overnight-iteration and one-line-patch-rebuild behavior is unchanged; (2) update the header comment block that advertises the \\\".build/ccache next to this repo\\\" default to match the new location; (3) do not write any log file into the repo — if a build log is wanted, send it to the same out-of-tree cache dir or leave it to the caller's redirection. Before finishing, delete the stray .build/ tree from the worktree (rm -rf .build) so nothing outside container/ and results/receipts/ is created, modified, or left uncommitted, then commit only container/ and results/receipts/ paths. The acceptance criterion recipe-pins is unaffected by this change: bash -n still passes and the grep-checked strings (torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch, mecattaf/vllm, flashnext:dev, MIT) all remain in place.\",\"taskId\":\"container-recipe\",\"verdict\":\"retry\"}],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787987412350}}
